            "encoding": "UTF-8",
            "tool": "Verbatim 2025-MUBandZauner-Afonso.tex extracted with GNU tar 1.34 from arXiv source archive SHA-256 99e0968bf51fbbb36ba8b3d3412e7dc6eb8c7f5a1b617fbb2acace2aeef08bdc"
          },
          "landing_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29571v1",
          "license": "CC BY 4.0",
          "locators": [
            {
              "excerpt": "    Two orthonormal bases $\\{v_1, \\dots, v_d\\}, \\{w_1, \\dots, w_d\\} \\subset \\mathbb{C}^d$ are called \\emph{mutually unbiased} if $|\\langle v_i, w_j \\rangle| = 1 / \\sqrt{d}$ for all $i, j$.",
              "excerpt_sha256": "c37b93c3899310cb2308802fc335173622f26120b84dc2bd3f2a98b07bba57d1",
              "label": "Definition 11.1",
              "page": 8,
              "purpose": "definition",
              "section": "Entry 11 Mutually Unbiased Bases, ETFs, and Zauner's Conjecture"
            },
            {
              "excerpt": "For $d$ not a prime power, the problem of determining $\\mathrm{MUB}(d)$ is still open. The smallest open instance is particularly well known for being a tantalizing open problem that has remained open (see Open Problem 6.2 in~\\cite{Afonso10L42P}).",
              "excerpt_sha256": "7e12a00a7bbbfab7f90238d8c9606031c632d76640860b363417a36a3936b524",
              "label": "Open-status paragraph before Conjecture 22",
              "page": 8,
              "purpose": "status",
              "section": "Entry 11 Mutually Unbiased Bases, ETFs, and Zauner's Conjecture"
            },
            {
              "excerpt": "    Let $\\mathrm{MUB}(d)$ denote the largest possible number of (simultaneously) mutually unbiased bases (MUBs) in $\\mathbb{C}^d$. We have $\\mathrm{MUB}(6)<7$.",
              "excerpt_sha256": "a8f7fdda72ee9d00b62b8119abed38ed82953703cffb83a255d89c915dd75ca4",
              "label": "Conjecture 22",
              "page": 8,
              "purpose": "statement",
              "section": "Entry 11 Mutually Unbiased Bases, ETFs, and Zauner's Conjecture"
            }
          ],
