      ],
      "target": "Prove that there do not exist vectors v_i^(k) in C^6, for 1<=i<=6 and 1<=k<=7, such that each {v_i^(k):1<=i<=6} is an orthonormal basis and, for every k!=l and every i,j, |<v_i^(k),v_j^(l)>|=1/sqrt(6); or give an exact construction of seven such bases and rigorously verify every required identity.",
      "title": "Seven mutually unbiased bases in complex dimension six"
    },
