            "encoding": "UTF-8",
            "tool": "Verbatim 2025-Paley-Afonso.tex extracted with GNU tar 1.34 from arXiv source archive SHA-256 99e0968bf51fbbb36ba8b3d3412e7dc6eb8c7f5a1b617fbb2acace2aeef08bdc"
          },
          "landing_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29571v1",
          "license": "CC BY 4.0",
          "locators": [
            {
              "excerpt": "Given a prime number $p$ such that $p \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$ the Paley graph on $p$ nodes $G_p$ is the graph where nodes $i$ and $j$ are connected if $i-j$ is a quadratic residue modulo $p$.",
              "excerpt_sha256": "d0825ddb2d3395cea96f84f19ce272301bc66492efe0883a0fa4b27304bbbe78",
              "label": "Paley graph definition",
              "page": 9,
              "purpose": "definition",
              "section": "Entry 12 On the clique number of the Paley Graph"
            },
            {
              "excerpt": "It was observed empirically in \\cite{MMP-2019-LPCliquesPaley} that $\\vartheta(\\overline{G_{p,1}}) \\sim \\sqrt{p/2}$",
              "excerpt_sha256": "ae87a8955a9bc90831ffef359f448c7651bf90414936a2cee62c4d49d3c74387",
              "label": "Empirical-status sentence before Conjecture 26",
              "page": 9,
              "purpose": "status",
              "section": "Entry 12 On the clique number of the Paley Graph"
